From a768c1f72efb8d70980def53f28e7dcca5e757f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] atbm6031: receive through NAPI with GRO

Each frame went up through netif_rx() as the SDIO RX thread read it,
so GRO had nothing to merge. As AltoBeam's newer SDK
(CONFIG_ATBM_SUPPORT_GRO), each interface queues its delivered frames
and a NAPI poll hands them to napi_gro_receive(): at the end of each
SDIO read pass, after a reorder timeout release, or once 64 are
queued. A poll that completes with frames queued behind its last
dequeue schedules itself again.
